[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-planting-decision :finalize-pruning-decision :authorize-pesticide-application :proceed-with-cultivation-work :override-nursery-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage" "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage" "2799009331-cloud-itonami-isco-9331-hand-and-pedal-vehicle-drivers-coverage" "2799009332-cloud-itonami-isco-9332-animal-drawn-vehicle-drivers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the planting work" "proceed with the pruning work" "proceed with the pesticide application" "finalize the planting decision" "finalize the pruning decision" "authorize the pesticide application" "finalize the pesticide application decision" "override the nursery safety officer's judgment" "override nursery safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799006113, :actor/domain :agriculture/nursery-horticulture-site-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:grower-verified :nursery-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "6113", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799006113: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 6113 Gardeners, Horticultural and Nursery Growers nursery scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 6113\n-- Gardeners, Horticultural and Nursery Growers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"6113\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"6113\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Gardeners, Horticultural and\nNursery Growers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this\nADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6113` (`gh\napi` 404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion\nregistry edit promote the `6113` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nGardeners, Horticultural and Nursery Growers work with cultivation\nequipment and agrochemicals -- real physical-safety stakes\n(pesticide/fertilizer chemical exposure, cultivation-tool/equipment\nhazards). The controlling constraint for this vertical is that the\nclosed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes\na cultivation-execution decision (e.g. deciding on a specific\nplanting, pruning or pesticide-application timing/technique), or\noverrides a nursery safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to NURSERY\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs\ncultivation work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, closest domain\nshape for a physical-safety trades vertical) -- cloned and read in\nfull in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6113` as an OSS nursery\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for gardeners, horticultural\nand nursery-grower crews, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Nursery Operations Advisor ⊣ NurseryOperationsGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **nursery scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct cultivation-execution authority** -- it must NEVER\nbe designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\ncultivation-execution decision (e.g. a specific planting, pruning or\npesticide-application timing/technique), or any override of a nursery\nsafety officer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- planting/pruning/harvest-record data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a chemical-exposure/equipment-hazard\n  concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- plants/seeds/agrochemicals procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\ncultivation-execution decision or a nursery-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-planting-decision` cannot even be proposed by the reference\nmock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one\nof the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a\nfuture LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the\ngovernor's closed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it\nunconditionally and permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names five concretely-forbidden ops\n(`nurseryops.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-planting-decision`, `:finalize-pruning-decision`,\n`:authorize-pesticide-application`, `:proceed-with-cultivation-work`,\n`:override-nursery-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and\nis verified by dedicated unit tests\n(`nurseryops.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-planting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pruning-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-pesticide-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-nursery-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Grower unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered grower record (`:no-grower`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the grower is.\n2. **Nursery unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered nursery site (`:no-nursery`). Together with check 1,\n   this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/nursery record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with planting,\n   pruning or pesticide-application work, or overriding a nursery\n   safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks cultivation-execution/safety-override language\n   wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a chemical-exposure/\n  equipment-hazard observation -- it never resolves the concern\n  itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard data,\"\n  never \"here is what I recommend doing about nursery safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  plants/seeds/agrochemicals order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  cultivation-execution or nursery-safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"planting\", \"pruning\", \"pesticide\", \"safety\") can accidentally match\ninside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a nursery coordination actor\nworking adjacent to planting/pruning/pesticide-application work\nnecessarily discusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job)\ncould trigger if phrased carelessly. `nurseryops.governor/scope-\nexcluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization/execution\nACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the pesticide application\", \"finalize the\nplanting decision\", \"override the nursery safety officer's judgment\"\n-- matching the task's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns,\nand `nurseryops.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-\nself-trip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test asserting\nevery op in the closed allowlist, driven through the default mock\nadvisor, never trips `:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own\ndefault rationale template was deliberately written to contain the\nbare nouns (\"logged work record for grower ...\", \"scheduled crew\noperation for planting task ...\", \"... routed for nursery safety\nofficer review\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`nurseryops.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"6113\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6113` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-6113`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately before\n  the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-planting-decision` or\n  `:approve-pesticide-application` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a cultivation-execution decision exists in\n  the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  this severe (chemical exposure, equipment hazard), the capability\n  itself must not exist. The only op related to nursery-safety\n  escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for\n  human/nursery-safety-officer attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a cultivation-execution decision for later\n  automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block: rejected per the task's\n  explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  plants/seeds/agrochemicals order is not itself unsafe, so it is\n  handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  cultivation-execution/nursery-safety-officer-override class is a\n  hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"planting\" \"pruning\"\n  \"pesticide\" \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked\n  example for this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to\n  phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS,\n  never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  planting/pruning/pesticide/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Splitting the nursery-safety-officer role into two roles (mirroring\n  cloud-itonami-isco-7111's site-safety-officer/foreman split):\n  rejected -- the task's domain design names a single \"nursery-safety\n  officer\" role only; introducing a second role not named in the task\n  would be scope creep without a corresponding real-world job title in\n  this occupation unit group.\n- Merging `grower` and `nursery` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered grower AND independently-registered\n  nursery) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/nursery\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- planting/pruning/harvest-record data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered grower AND\n   nursery (`:no-grower`/`:no-nursery`). Not a cultivation-execution\n   or nursery-safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a cultivation-execution decision (structurally\n   absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt via free text is\n   caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not\n   authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific\n   planting, pruning or pesticide-application step -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a chemical-exposure/\n   equipment-hazard concern to a human/nursery safety officer; ALWAYS\n   escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the nursery safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- plants/seeds/agrochemicals\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a cultivation-execution\n   or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na cultivation-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\nplanting, pruning or pesticide-application timing/technique) or a\nnursery-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`nurseryops.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`nurseryops.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`nurseryops.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-planting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pruning-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-pesticide-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-nursery-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`nurseryops.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a pesticide application or override a\nnursery safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`nurseryops.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-proceed-with-pesticide-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-nursery-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Nursery & Horticultural Site Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :grower-verification :nursery-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-6113", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6113", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6113], :test/simulator :nurseryops.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-6113 — Gardeners, Horticultural and Nursery Growers Nursery Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-6113}]